{"name":"Black Mesa","hex":"#222211","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Black Mesa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An upland area in Apache County and Navajo County, Arizona, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Black_Mesa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Mesa (Oklahoma, Colorado, New Mexico)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Mesa is a mesa located in an area covering parts of the U.S. states of Colorado, New Mexico, and Oklahoma. It extends from Mesa de Maya, Colorado southeasterly 28 miles (45 km) crossing into the northeast corner of New Mexico, and ending in the Oklahoma panhandle along the north bank of the Cimarron River at its confluence with the North Carrizo Creek near Kenton. Its highest elevation is 5,705 feet (1,739 m) in Colorado. The highest point of Black Mesa within New Mexico is 5,239 feet (1,597 m). In northwestern Cimarron County, Oklahoma, Black Mesa reaches 4,973 feet (1,516 m), the highest point in the state of Oklahoma. The plateau that formed at the top of the mesa has been known as a \"geological wonder\" of North America. There is abundant wildlife in this shortgrass prairie environment, including mountain lions, butterflies, and the Texas horned lizard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Black_Mesa_summit%2C_Oklahoma.jpg/330px-Black_Mesa_summit%2C_Oklahoma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Mesa_(Oklahoma%2C_Colorado%2C_New_Mexico)","wikidata":"Q880398"},{"title":"Black Mesa Test Range","blocks":[{"text":"Black Mesa was a rocket testing facility of the US Army in Utah. Many rockets of the Pershing type have been launched for testing from Black Mesa between 1963 and 1971. It was located in what is now the Utah Test and Training Range (UTTR) which was taken over by the Air Force Systems Command in 1979."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Mesa_Test_Range","wikidata":"Q578698"},{"title":"Black Mesa (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Mesa is a 2020 first-person shooter video game developed and published by Crowbar Collective. It is a fan-made remake of Half-Life (1998) in the Source game engine. Originally published as a free mod in September 2012, Black Mesa was approved for commercial release by Valve, the developers of Half-Life. The first commercial version was published as an early-access release in May 2015 with an abridged campaign, followed by a full release in March 2020 restoring the final chapters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/Black_Mesa_release_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Mesa_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q211229"},{"title":"Mesa","blocks":[{"text":"A mesa is an isolated, flat-topped elevation, ridge, or hill, bounded from all sides by steep escarpments and standing distinctly above a surrounding plain. Mesas consist of flat-lying soft sedimentary rocks, such as shales, capped by a resistant layer of harder rock, like sandstone or limestone, forming a caprock that protects the flat summit. The caprock may also include dissected lava flows or eroded duricrust."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg/330px-Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa","wikidata":"Q623319"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Crotalus_viridis_oreganus02.jpg/500px-Crotalus_viridis_oreganus02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Crotalus_viridis_oreganus02.jpg/500px-Crotalus_viridis_oreganus02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The prairie rattlesnake is well adapted to Black Mesa's dry environment.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrotalus_viridis_oreganus02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg/500px-P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg/1280px-P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg/500px-P1030326_copy_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Papilio polyxenes, the state butterfly of Oklahoma, is found on Black Mesa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP1030326_copy_filtered.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Black_Mesa_and_Half-Life_comparison%2C_anomalous_materials%2C_lobby_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Black_Mesa_and_Half-Life_comparison%2C_anomalous_materials%2C_lobby_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Comparison of the Anomalous Materials lobby room in Half-Life (top) and Black Mesa (bottom)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Mesa_and_Half-Life_comparison%2C_anomalous_materials%2C_lobby_room.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ec/Half_Life-Surface_Tension.jpg/330px-Half_Life-Surface_Tension.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ec/Half_Life-Surface_Tension.jpg/330px-Half_Life-Surface_Tension.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%